Z||000000||Kwez||07-29-2001||09:39 PM||||hi,<BR>I (a friend actually) just changed the front rotors & pads (KVR performance pads) on my 88GT.<BR>first, it was a b$tch, it took 2.5hrs for the left front wheel !! he couldn't believe how long it took, he did his on a 84 a few times in the past & never had so much trouble.<P>anyways, on the driver's side, the caliper was very difficult to put back on, the pads were too tight on the rotor. (as far as I know the piston is a far in as it can go)<BR>we hoped that it would be ok after driving a bit ...<BR>but after driving the car back to my place, we notice the wheel is hot !<BR>I think the rotor might even be warped now, I tried driving it a 2nd at night (cooler) & checked the wheel & yep, it got hot again pretty quick, so I parked the dagn thing.<P>Can I use some rough sandpaper to wear down the pads so I can drive my car !! ??<BR>Any ideas / tricks ??<P>thx<BR>Getting a bit fed-up (same day, my 'for sale' 87GT overheated !!)||||reg||5
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||07-29-2001||11:24 PM||||sounds like your calipers are sticking you will need to rebuild them or replace them with rebuilt ones I would replace them myself.allthe sanding in the world is not going to take care of this problem,as soon as you apply the brakes the piston will hang up again .I just had a thought though were your brakes working properly before you guys changed the pads? If so it might you guys did not install the bushings on the caliper properly.do the bushings on the calipers slide on the O-Rings with some grease on the O-Rings of course ?Hmmmmlet us know why it took 2 hours do the frnt brakes was it the piston that was hanging up on ?in the caliper||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kwez||07-30-2001||01:50 AM||||the pads on the rigth wheel looked almost new, but the ones on the left (the 'hot' one) were almost completely gone, maybe that's an indication there was a prob to begin with.<P>the brakes were not very good when I got the car, I could tell there was some warped rotors (in the back probably) & there was not much braking power, that's why I got the brakes done. I still have to have someone do the rear end brakes.<P>bushings ? o-rings ? sorry I'm mechanically challenged ;-)<BR>the two 'cylinders' (o-rings ?) that slide inside the caliper were jammed stiff. that was a big part of why it took so long to do that wheel. they were 'unjammed', cleaned & greased (synthetic for the heat).<P>the cylinder itself was also pretty difficult to push in. <BR>like i said before, the caliper was very difficult to put back on for that wheel because it was very tight (pads on the rotor), at first we could not put it back on at all.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||07-30-2001||08:22 AM||||Hey Kwez!<BR>First off, you need to replace both the rotors and the calipers...<BR>Go with rebuilt calipers, as rebuilding them is questionable with out the proper tools..<BR>They could end up sticking after rebuilding if it isn't done right...<BR>Also change your brake hoses, as they deteriorate too...<BR>You will have excelent braking afterwards, if you do this to the car...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Kwez||07-30-2001||02:18 PM||||ok, thx.<P>this is getting expensive !!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>how can I know if I need to replace the calipers in the back too ?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Roy Grooms||08-09-2001||12:34 PM|||| YA ,they are right, i just got done replaceing all 4 wheels calb. hoses pads, and cut the rotors on my 84 2m4. now its time bleeding them. my sons coming over to be the pedal pumper ,the old way, most of the time you need all four done<BR>     Roys/toy||||reg||1
Z||000006||starfighter007@msn.com||08-09-2001||12:46 PM||||I suppose you would make sure that they are wareing evenly, If not and or they are very thin The pads that is do not do any thing with out checking with us first so we can guide you thru this. Rear disc brakes can be difficult if you have never done them before but simple proscess if you know what you are doing or with proper guidence. let us know ||||reg||4
Z||000007||Kwez||08-09-2001||03:31 PM||||... almost there !!!!<P>I finally went back to a garage (they had a tie rod to install for me) to put on new calipers in front & install the new rotors & pads in the rear.<P>I got the car back two days ago, it still doesn't brake any better than before (I was told it should get better as the pads 'wear even') <BR>& <BR>the rear driver's side goes tick tick tick tick, a bit like a warped rotor.<BR>(and I'm going "sh$t sh$t sh$t sh$t sh$t " ;-)<P>getting very frustrated here !<BR>one step forward, two steps back.<P>Gotta remove the rotor & clean its back side & wheel, i hope it'll fix the prob (friend had same prob in the past & fixed it that way: some rust/dirt kept the rotor from being properly aligned)<P>- Fierowrecker, <BR>"change the brake hoses", <BR>do you mean the flexible rubber part or the whole lines ?<BR>I had asked the shop to install steel [braided] lines while they were at it, they said; "no prob we make 'em ourselves" ... ??<BR>turns out he thought I meant the lines not the rubber hose part, so ... that didn't happen.<BR>The rubber hoses LOOK like they're in good shape. Not cracked, still very flexible.<P>can't wait to be able to drive the darn thing !||||reg||7
Z||000008||Kwez||08-11-2001||12:08 AM||||finally...<P>steps/kweztions taken/asked :<P>1) as mentionned above cleaned the 3 surfaces (back of rotor, wheel hub face (? where the rotor sits), back of wheel (where it contacts w. front of rotor)<P>there was some rust/dirt, thought it might fix the prob ...<P>but no, same difference (ie NO difference)<P>2a) brand new rotor is deffect ?<BR>2b) some oil on the rotor ?<BR>2c) other suspect: 'joint homocynetic' (have no idea what the english name is for that, sorry). that's the articulated arms from the trans to the wheel (that transmit the power)<P>so<P>3a) re-install brakes/wheel, <BR>3b) test brakes again w. trans to Neutral ...<BR>still 'vibrates' ... so 'homo joint' not culprit.<P>4) sounds like rotor maybe, so:<BR>4b) decide to swap rear rotors left &lt;-&gt; right to confirm if rotor is bad ...<P>5) WTF ?? everything is OK now (my friend wasn't surprised, said he's seen this before !)<P>so I can finally drive my car !<P>thank you everybody !||||reg||6
